Feature:

Background: This executes once per feature file
	Given these properties
		|cmis.repository.type|documentum6|
		|custom.properties|session.store.password=true${line.separator}company.security.auth.type=screenName|
		|osgi.app.includes|documentum|
		|portal.release|true|
		|portal.upstream|true|
		|test.run.environment|EE|
		|testray.main.component.name|Documents Management|

Setup: This executes before each scenario 
	Given TestCase set Up Portal Instance
	When these variables
		|documentumVMHostName|TestPropsUtil#get('cmis.repository.vm.host.name')|
	And AntCommand the value 'clean-documentum-repository -Dssh.host=${documentumVMHostName}' at locator 'build-test-documentum.xml'
	And User login PG
		|authenticationMethod|By Screen Name|
		|userScreenName|test|
	And Page goto My Account
		|portletName|Account Settings|
	And User edit Details Via My Account
		|userScreenNameEdit|barthur|
	And Page goto My Account
		|portletName|Account Settings|
	And User edit Password Via My Account
		|currentPassword|test|
		|newPassword|barthur|
	And User logout PG
	And User login PG
		|authenticationMethod|By Screen Name|
		|password|barthur|
		|userScreenName|barthur|
	And Navigator open URL
	And ProductMenu goto Sites Content
		|portlet|Documents and Media|
	And DMNavigator goto Add Repository CP
	And DMRepository edit
		|dmRepositoryName|Documentum Repository Name|
	And DMRepository add Documentum
		|dmCabinetName|Wombat Insurance Co|
		|dmRepositoryFieldName|documentum|
	And PortletEntry save
	And ProductMenuHelper close Product Menu
	And DMRepository goto CP
		|dmRepositoryName|Documentum Repository Name|
	And DMFolder view CP
		|dmFolderName|Claim Templates|
	And Navigator open URL
	And ProductMenu goto Sites Content
		|portlet|Documents and Media|
	And ProductMenuHelper close Product Menu
	And DMRepository goto CP
		|dmRepositoryName|Documentum Repository Name|
	And DMFolder view CP
		|dmFolderName|Filed Claims|
	And Navigator open URL
	And ProductMenu goto Sites Content
		|portlet|Documents and Media|
	Then ProductMenuHelper close Product Menu

Teardown: This executes after each scenario 
	Given PortalInstances tear Down CP
		|testPortalInstance|TestPropsUtil#get('test.portal.instance')|
